comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T19:07:23.916Z",codex-agent,"Imported GitHub #241 with the pinned importer. This draft starts from main and carries the engine side of #240: buffered and streaming worktree capture, refs and GC, control JSON, object and pack reads, erasure and destruction records, and publication/recovery metadata. Both branches regenerate the bundle. Review this draft after #240 merges."
  "2026-11-26T19:13:02.294Z",codex-agent,"Transferred engine revert proofs from the combined branch. Removing descriptor identity validation admitted replaced native working-file bytes in the non-Git staging fixture. Restoring pathname control reads consumed nonregular replacements. Rechecking pathname presence after parsing turned captured JSON null into absence in both native state tests. Removing each pre-read or post-read refusal admitted a changed destruction intent, a nonregular lease audit descriptor, or premature object EOF in separate isolated reverts. The six corresponding cases pass on this independent branch."
  "2026-11-26T19:33:45.678Z",codex-agent,"The focused engine tests and the pinned PM linked test passed 6/6. After building the fresh worktree, bisect passed 56/56 and the full-depth packed composition consumer passed 6/6 with built and installed Node, Bun 1.3.14, and the real project-installed CLI. Two erasure crash cases selected the default four internal workers during the first sweep. Both cases passed again under one CPU with one internal worker, covering 9 and 25 selected crash cuts."
  "2026-11-26T19:35:22.672Z",codex-agent,"The targeted sweep passed 923 of 925 with no skips or cancellations. The two failures required the missing built dist in the fresh checkout. Both passed after the build: bisect 56/56 and the packed consumer 6/6. Typecheck, source and test builds, lint, duplication 0%, docstrings, and pack privacy with 369 files and zero findings passed. Exact-head CI is tracked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=branch%3Afix%2Fengine-opened-descriptor-reads ."
